    "input": "search_document: Hello! Thank you for your question. I am happy to help clarify the refund timeline for you.\n\nBased on the Northwind Outdoor handbook, here are the details regarding your refund:\n\n**Refund Timing for Credit Cards**\nYes, you read correctly. For **credit and debit cards**, refunds typically appear on your statement within **5 to 10 business days** after we process the return [payments.5]. Since you specified you are using a credit card, this timeframe applies to you.\n\n**Additional Processing Time**\nPlease note that you should allow an **additional 3 business days** for your bank to post the credit after we have initiated the refund [payments.5]. This means the total time from when we process the return until the money is fully available in your account could be up to 13 business days (10 days for the statement update + 3 days for the bank posting).\n\n**Do You Need to Do Anything Special with Your Bank?**\nThe handbook does not list any specific actions you need to take with your bank to receive the refund. However, it does note that if you are an international customer, you should verify with your bank that they support cross-border transactions to avoid issues, though this is primarily mentioned in the context of making payments rather than receiving refunds [payments.3]. Since the refund is issued to the **original payment method only** [payments.5], no special setup is required for the refund itself, but you may want to check with your bank if they have any specific holds or delays for international refunds.\n\n**Important Notes**\n*   Refunds are issued to the original payment method only [payments.5].\n*   We do not issue refunds as cash or to different payment methods [payments.5].\n*   The 5\u201310 business day window starts **after** we process the return, not necessarily the day you ship it back. You will need to wait for us to receive and process the item first.\n\nI hope this helps you plan for your next trip! If you have any other questions, feel free to ask.",
    "model": "nomic-embed-text",
